1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,220
Listen to a talk in an anthropology class.

2
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:11,397
Man: In the first half of the 20th century,

3
00:00:11,397 --> 00:00:17,150
an anthropological movement emerged, called the Culture and Personality School.

4
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:20,845
According to the Culture and Personality school,

5
00:00:20,845 --> 00:00:26,651
people's personalities are a result of the culture they live in,

6
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:34,040
and not just based on biology, like not just inherited from their biological parents.

7
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:38,427
For example, how children in a culture experience food,

8
00:00:38,427 --> 00:00:41,480
the foods they eat, how it's prepared

9
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:45,250
this shapes their individual tastes and preferences.

10
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:51,290
One of the anthropologists most associated with this movement was Ruth Benedict.

11
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:58,140
Benedict studied and embraced the principles of cultural relativism.

12
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:00,764
So according to cultural relativism,

13
00:01:00,764 --> 00:01:05,320
all cultures should be studied on their own terms

14
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:09,160
and not judged against some external measure.

15
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:11,567
So cultures in, say, Egypt,

16
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:19,270
belong to Egypt and shouldn't be the standard of what all cultures should try to be.

17
00:01:19,270 --> 00:01:24,844
Ruth Benedict refuted the dominant anthropology theory at the time,

18
00:01:24,844 --> 00:01:32,090
which stated that there was a hierarchy of cultures, some advanced, others not.

19
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:34,250
Rejecting that took courage.

20
00:01:34,250 --> 00:01:37,240
And I think the field is better for it.

21
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:44,150
Benedict was also influenced by psychology, especially Gestalt ideas.

22
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:50,020
According to Gestalt psychology, a personality is an integrated whole

23
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:53,030
not just a list of traits.

24
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:56,677
Like, If you see a painting of a landscape,

25
00:01:56,677 --> 00:02:03,160
you're looking at a whole landscape and not just say, a hill, trees and a farmhouse.

26
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:07,769
Benedict said that cultures were the same way,

27
00:02:07,769 --> 00:02:10,920
a whole coherent system with patterns of values

28
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:18,140
and behaviors, and more than just a set of characteristics.
